      "id": "p2",
      "description": "M1 denominator $1 + (2\\cos^2\\theta - 1) = 2\\cos^2\\theta$.",
      "marks": 1
     },
     {
      "id": "p3",
      "description": "A1 cancels to $\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta} = \\tan\\theta$.",
      "marks": 1
     }
    ]
   },
   "modelAnswer": "$$\n\\frac{\\sin 2\\theta}{1 + \\cos 2\\theta} = \\frac{2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}{1 + 2\\cos^2\\theta - 1} = \\frac{2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}{2\\cos^2\\theta} = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta} = \\tan\\theta\n$$"
